 "docs": {
  "en": {
   "title": "Alpine meadows snow conditions: Where to find the best snow in the US West now (21 November)",
   "description": "Snow on the ground, snow from the last 72 hours, snow still to come: together they point to Kirkwood, Bear Valley and Dodge Ridge. Among these …",
   "lede": "Alpine meadows snow conditions – Snow on the ground, snow from the last 72 hours, snow still to come: together they point to Kirkwood, Bear Valley and Dodge Ridge. Among these resorts, Palisades Tahoe Alpine Meadows holds the most snow on its upper slopes today, about 46 in (116 cm), followed by Bear Valley 44 in (111 cm) and Kirkwood 43 in (109 cm). Every number here is an estimate with some uncertainty; the trend over several days is usually more reliable than one value.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Snow still to come",
     "p": [
      "More snow, and so more stored water, is on the way: by 24 November our forecast gives 2 in (4 cm) at Kirkwood, 2 in (4 cm) at Bear Valley and 1 in (3 cm) at Dodge Ridge.",
      "Forecasts a few days ahead can change: look at the map again the day before you travel."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Against past winters",
     "p": [
      "At about 8,638 ft (2,633 m), Kirkwood has 44 in (111 cm) today; a normal 21 November has 9 in (22 cm) there.",
      "That is more than in 45 of the 46 past winters on this date.",
      "In past winters the best snow at Kirkwood usually came early January / early March.",
      "An early lead like this matters most for the lower and middle runs, which usually wait until December for this much snow.",
      "Day by day at Kirkwood: Sunday 22 November 1 in (2 cm); Monday 23 November 1 in (2 cm).",
      "Height by height at Kirkwood: 7,815 ft (2,382 m) 39 in (99 cm) on the ground, 5 in (12 cm) more in the next 7 days; 8,638 ft (2,633 m) 45 in (114 cm) on the ground, 6 in (14 cm) more in the next 7 days; 9,462 ft (2,884 m) 45 in (115 cm) on the ground, 6 in (14 cm) more in the next 7 days."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Height and the snow line",
     "p": [
      "With the freezing level at 1,444 ft (440 m) to 7,316 ft (2,230 m) on 21 November, below the base of Kirkwood, any precipitation should fall as snow and stay on the mountain.",
      "Shade protects the snowpack. High, north-facing slopes get less sun, so their snow lasts longer than on the south side."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Safety and avalanche level",
     "p": [
      "Today the official avalanche danger for the Kirkwood area is 3 on the 5-level scale (avalanche.org (US national portal)).",
      "Before you ski off-piste or go touring, read the official avalanche bulletin (links below)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Where the snow is best",
     "p": [
      "In the last 72 hours, 25 in (63 cm) of new snow fell on Kirkwood. Height changes everything at Kirkwood: our model gives 39 in (99 cm) at the base (7,815 ft / 2,382 m), 45 in (114 cm) at mid-mountain (8,638 ft / 2,633 m) and 45 in (115 cm) at the top (9,462 ft / 2,884 m). On 17 November, its last clear day, satellites saw snow covering Kirkwood.",
      "Bear Valley gained 24 in (60 cm) of new snow in the last 72 hours. Our model splits Bear Valley into three heights: 44 in (112 cm) at the top (8,484 ft / 2,586 m), 37 in (94 cm) at mid-mountain (7,562 ft / 2,305 m), 32 in (82 cm) at the base (6,640 ft / 2,024 m). The last clear satellite view of Bear Valley, on 17 November, shows the slopes covered in snow.",
      "In the last 72 hours, 25 in (63 cm) of new snow fell on Dodge Ridge. Height changes everything at Dodge Ridge: our model gives 28 in (70 cm) at the base (6,568 ft / 2,002 m), 33 in (83 cm) at mid-mountain (7,356 ft / 2,242 m) and 43 in (108 cm) at the top (8,143 ft / 2,482 m). On 17 November, its last clear day, satellites saw snow covering Dodge Ridge."
     ]
    }
   ],
   "advice": [
    "Snow on the map does not mean a resort is open: check lifts and opening dates on the resort's website.",
    "Small ski areas next to the big names often get the same storm and shorter lift lines. Check them on the map first.",
    "Early-season snow is thin. Stay on open, groomed pistes: rocks and grass can hide just under the surface.",
    "South-facing slopes take the most sun and melt first; high, north-facing slopes keep their snow the longest.",
    "Get a powder alert in the SnowScope app to know when Kirkwood gets fresh snow."
   ],
   "captions": {
    "map": "Snow depth in the US West on 21 November 2026 (SnowScope snow model): Kirkwood, Bear Valley, Dodge Ridge, Palisades Tahoe Alpine Meadows."
   }
  }
